WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:06.160
David, do you think Joe Biden has&nbsp;
any shot at passing that tax plan?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:13.040
So we talked about this a little bit last week&nbsp;
with Nick Majilis from Ritholtz Wealth Management.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:18.560
I think that there's two scenarios. Without&nbsp;
the Senate, it's just a hard no. I don't see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:26.320
how on earth Joe Biden gets a tax reform done if&nbsp;
he doesn't have the Senate. Now with the Senate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:29.840
you've got a debate. And what's really&nbsp;
important for many of you to understand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:36.240
is that Joe Biden, although he may be to&nbsp;
your right, has put out a tax plan that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.240 --> 00:00:42.080
is well to the left of many Senate Democrats&nbsp;
who Joe Biden would need to pass tax reform.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:47.840
There are many on the left who are upset that&nbsp;
Joe Biden has no wealth tax in his tax plan.&nbsp;

00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:53.520
A wealth tax is not popular among Senate Democrats&nbsp;
if and until the Senate becomes far more left than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:58.480
it is right now. A wealth tax has no chance&nbsp;
of passing whatsoever. So you are going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:03.840
see if Joe Biden gets the Senate. You'll see some&nbsp;
provisions that are likely to pass, for example,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.840
a return of the top marginal tax rate&nbsp;
to thirty nine point six percent. It was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:12.320
dropped to 36 percent or maybe thirty seven.&nbsp;
Thirty six. Thirty seven under Donald Trump.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:18.160
That would almost certainly go back to thirty nine&nbsp;
point six percent. It is seen by the Democratic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:23.760
establishment and to be frank, by some in the&nbsp;
Republican establishment as something that on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:29.200
paper looks nice, were raising the top tax rate&nbsp;
for the richest people. Many people who are in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:36.160
that top tax rate are not earning money through&nbsp;
wages anyway, so they are not subject to that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:43.760
You will almost certainly see that uncapping&nbsp;
Social Security at four hundred thousand dollars.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.760 --> 00:01:48.320
I think there's no way in hell that that&nbsp;
passes, not because of Joe Biden, but because of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:54.000
Senate Democrats, as you may know right now, you&nbsp;
pay Social Security tax or you and your employer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:54.000 --> 00:02:01.200
pay Social Security tax on the first 130000 or&nbsp;
so dollars in earnings. And then Social Security&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:05.840
tax goes to zero. Once you get past that one&nbsp;
hundred and thirty thousand, whether you make&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:11.760
two hundred thousand a year, a million, 10 million&nbsp;
a year, you pay zero. Once you get past that cap,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:19.920
Joe Biden's proposal is at 400000 plus the tax&nbsp;
kicks back in and it goes uncapped. I think there&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:24.960
is no way in hell that Senate Democrats passed&nbsp;
that Senate Democrats are just too conservative to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:32.240
see that happen, the increase in the capital gains&nbsp;
tax rate. I think that that is a 50/50, but that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:38.080
there are ways it gets done with some negotiation.&nbsp;
And then I think that the stepped up basis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:44.880
provision that Joe Biden wants to eliminate is&nbsp;
probably a long shot. I won't explain it all now&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.880 --> 00:02:50.960
because I've explained it in a number of previous&nbsp;
videos. Will there be a new higher tax bracket?&nbsp;

00:02:50.960 --> 00:02:57.600
So even if you raise the top tax bracket from&nbsp;
thirty seven to thirty nine point six percent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:04.000
as Joe Biden wants to do, many progressive&nbsp;
economists and lawmakers say, well, we need&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:09.680
we need a higher tax bracket. Fine. You get into&nbsp;
the highest tax bracket at five hundred thousand a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:14.240
year in income, but when you get to two&nbsp;
million a year in income, then it should&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.240 --> 00:03:21.040
go to 43 percent. And when you get to five million&nbsp;
a year in income, it should go to 48 percent and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:28.720
so on. You could have that configured a number of&nbsp;
different ways. I would be shocked if we saw that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:36.240
again, because the Democratic Party in&nbsp;
the Senate right now is well to the right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:45.840
of where Joe Biden has run. And that's my thought&nbsp;
on the major provisions of Joe Biden's tax plan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.720 --> 00:03:53.440
If Democrats take the Senate, I just don't see any&nbsp;
path forward. If Democrats don't take the Senate.&nbsp;

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:56.960
If you disagree with me, let me know.&nbsp;
I want to hear from you. We've got a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:00.000
great bonus show for you today.
Remember, the number one way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:07.280
to access the bonus show is to grab a membership&nbsp;
at Join Pakman Dotcom. Do it. I'll see you then.

